_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 4
---
order: 4
---
short_label: VIII.4
---
red_highlight: yes
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Given as many ratios as we please in least numbers, to find numbers in continued proportion which are the least in the given ratios.
----
proof:

Let the given ratios in least numbers be that of {A} to {B}, that of {C} to {D}, and that of {E} to {F}.

It is required to find numbers in continued proportion which are the least that are in the ratio of {A} to {B}, in the ratio of {C} to {D}, and in the ratio of {E} to {F}.

